  {
    "episode_id": 75023,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75023.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 49,
    "turn_text": "I don't know what, you know, 20 years, 10 years ago, you used to get people in companies out, raise their hands, say, okay, I want to move to Beijing or Shanghai or whatever, and move to their offices. You can't get anybody in Japan, Europe or et cetera, or the United States. Employees raise their hands, say, I'd like to move my family to a city where I could get arrested any given day and be in lockdown. So they have now lost the confidence of the world. What he did and rising youth unemployment massively declining foreign investment. And China did not lift hundreds of millions of people out of poverty. The international system that China was a part of enabled China to do that. They followed smart policies at home. The international system of which they were probably the singular greatest beneficiary, they walked turned their back on. And when they turned their back on, guess what? The rest of the world started to turn or at least the developer that they cared about started turning their back. Okay, how many times are you going to have somebody just turn their back on you? How many times you're going to have somebody steal your intellectual property or create economic espionage or arrest your citizens, cavalierly. So I think our desire would be, if you want to come back into the system, be part of a responsible stakeholder, have your voice heard and contribute. Great. If you want to turn your back on it and be self-sufficient to the point that the rest of the world is literally pushed away, that you'll have the own domestic consequences in China. And that's the part of China that they're most scared about. They're scared of the United States. They're scared of the neighborhood, a collective unified neighbor. They're very scared of the Chinese people. And they have a reason to be scared of the Chinese people because they have failed to deliver the very fundamental premise. You give us security and power. We'll give you the access to the Chinese dream and they have crushed it.",
