    "turn_idx": 52,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's not in our interests. I didn't say it was ever. They made a choice and it has consequences. In China, they're arresting their entrepreneurs. They're pushing them out of the country. Facts. The number fourth ethnic group that is coming at the southwest border, coming over the southwest border of the United States is Chinese. That's a $30,000 trip. That is not the rural poor of China. Here in, somebody told me I don't know if it would be true or not true. Here in Japan and Tokyo, any apartment or condo above $2 million has a Chinese bidder on it. They're the major real estate buyer in Hokkaido. People are getting their money out. They're leaving. Entrepreneurs are not starting businesses. Youth unemployment, whether they want to report accurate data or not, it doesn't change the fact that there's a high propensity of unemployed youth in China. Capital is fleeing. So at some point, and there was 10 years ago a different economic structure in China. It wasn't just built on debt. It was built on entrepreneurship. It was built on the world having confidence in China's future and willing to invest in it. China decided not to have that. Okay. I can't stop you from hurting yourself. I tried, but you won't listen.",
