  {
    "episode_id": 75023,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75023.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, part of the leadership is knowing what you can do and what you can't do. The price in China right now is cognizant on the Chinese. They know the economy is not doing well. They know their youth are unemployed. They know that people aren't getting homes. They know the fact is that the next, the future generation has very little confidence in the Chinese dream where the Chinese Communist Party is able to deliver. That's going to be one of the biggest holds on China. I've always said there's three China's. There's a core China. It's called the three C's. The core is calm. The relationship between the PRC and the people of China, they want calm and they're very nervous about it. The second ring is the conflict ring, which is China in the neighborhood, India, Philippines, Japan. They're in constant conflict. And then there's the outer outer ring, which is what they call the charm China. It's a win-win. We just want people to get along, et cetera. And all those are in conflict with each other. I mean, by way of example, China's trying to convince our Western business leaders to invest in China so they can have the calm China yet. We just discovered not only ourselves with the UK, incredible cyber attacks generated by the Chinese government in our two respective countries. That's the conflict China. And the conflict in China are not the same. Or as I like to say yesterday, they're very, very charming and they're very frequently offensive.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Leadership involves knowing your capabilities and limitations.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The current economic situation in China is perceived negatively by the Chinese population.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Chinese youth face high levels of unemployment.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Many Chinese citizens cannot afford housing.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The younger generation in China lacks confidence in the Chinese Dream as delivered by the CCP.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The lack of faith in the Chinese Dream represents a significant challenge for China.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "China consists of three distinct layers: the core, the conflict ring, and the charm ring.",
        "confidence": 0.84
      },
      {
        "text": "The core China is characterized by a desire for stability and peace.",
        "confidence": 0.83
      },
      {
        "text": "The conflict ring includes tensions with neighboring countries such as India, the Philippines, and Japan.",
        "confidence": 0.82
      },
      {
        "text": "Charm China promotes a narrative of mutual benefit and global harmony.",
