    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75023.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 116,
    "turn_text": "I think it's just, I think it's total BS. There's no such thing as quality time. There is time present with a child that's valuable versus other time, but it's not quality time. You can't box off something. We did little things like we made an effort more right than wrong, more consistent than the incuses and the four dinners a night as a family, Shabbat, Sunday nights and the two during the week. No matter when I was either mayor, chief of staff, et cetera. We used to have Summer reading list and at the end of the summer you had to do a book You had to do a dinner where you kind of reported on the book you read and let a discussion of the family We used to always we took when I was mayor chief of staff I got in trouble when I was mayor, but I didn't care We always for 20 years consistently mid-March passing it took a family vacation So my job wasn't always impacting the family and I was more a father than I was either mayor chief of staff and always being disturbed I think there's, when our kids were doing homework, I would do my reading in one of their rooms, so you were present. It wasn't a forced type of thing. There's other things to do. I mean, I took each child on a just one of the children in myself on a holiday. So there was no appellate court, there was no sibling",
