    "turn_idx": 118,
    "turn_text": "And then I think probably the most important, those are the little tactical things. The most important thing is build a home of love. And if you have love, an education, a kid will survive and thrive. I think we underappreciate. My dad used to have this phrase, and I think the more I think about it, he's never met a child that was spoiled because you told them you love them too many times a day. If you could give them, not just tell them, but show them that you love them, not buy them things, but you appreciate them. I think the rest of it takes care of itself. It's very complicated, but",
